.SH NAME
kamcmd \- kamailio command line tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kamcmd
[
.B options
]
[
.B command
[
.B arguments
]
]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kamcmd
is a command line to interact with
.B Kamailio SIP server
It can be used to manage users, domains, aliases and other server options.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP 12
.B \-h
display a short usage description, including all available options.
.TP
.BI \-s " address"
use the specified Unix or IP socket.
.TP
.B \-b
use the binrpc protocol (the default).
.TP
.B \-j
use the JSON-RPC protocol. With no command, enter interactive mode and load
RPC command names for readline completion using system.listMethods.
.TP
.B \-p
pretty-print JSON-RPC responses. Raw JSON output remains the default.
.TP
.B \-y
print JSON-RPC responses in a compact YAML-style form.
.TP
.BI \-t " timeout"
set the JSON-RPC response timeout in seconds.
.TP
.BI \-z " size"
set the JSON-RPC response buffer size in kilobytes.

.SH NOTE
.B kamcmd
tries to convert number parameters to integer, to avoid it, prefix the number
with
.B 's:'
, like
.B 's:123456789'.

.SH AUTHORS

see
.B /usr/share/doc/kamailio/AUTHORS

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kamailio(8),
.BR kamailio.cfg(5)
.PP
